{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480373-2e-homebrew-legacy-the-crawlers-of-yggdrasil","id":1480373,"title":"[2e Homebrew Legacy] The Crawlers of Yggdrasil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-07T10:38:20-07:00","id":1480373,"title":"[2e Homebrew Legacy] The Crawlers of Yggdrasil","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>The Crawlers of Yggdrasil</b></u></span><br /> <br /> Determining the history of any Legacy associated with time travel is a difficult proposition. With how many changes have been made to the timeline over the years, getting an exact year or even century for its founding is nigh impossible. This is not helped by the fact that the Founder, according to the Legacy\u2019s membership, deliberately did all they could to obfuscate the point of origin for both parts security and amusement. Further confusing matters is the diffuse nature of the Legacy\u2019s members, both across space and particularly time. As such, the Crawlers of Yggdrasil have only their mythology and what they <i>believe</i> to be the point of origin with what facts they have on hand.<br /> It is suggested that the Crawlers originated in either Scandinavia or Central Europe, sometime after the Christianization of those places. What history the Crawlers have been able to divine or retain states that the founder was either a historian or a storyteller pre-15<sup>th</sup> century that lamented the loss of many of their people\u2019s legends after massive conversions to Christianity. They set out to study the corridors of time, but were unsure of exactly how to do so. It was what little of their people\u2019s history that remained which inspired them to create this legacy.<br /> In Norse myth, there is an ash tree which extends across the cosmos, connecting nine different worlds together as one collective system. At the top of the tree lies an eagle, and at its roots lay the serpent Nidhogg, with an expanse of bark and branches in-between. It was the role of the squirrel Ratatoskr to ferry messages across the length of the tree to various individuals, but particularly the eagle and the serpent as they were so distant from one another. Of course, being as mischievous as he is, Ratatoskr used this task to also spread gossip regarding the other to each destination, enraging those who heard his words.<br /> The founder of the Crawlers used this myth as a model for time travel: The World Tree represents the main timeline, with the branches and worlds attached to it as expanding branches of time or even separate timelines altogether. The eagle, with its great knowledge over all, represents the future in its infinite possibility. The serpent, then, represents the past, devouring the roots of time to prevent them from being traveled to further. The mage must in turn represent Ratatoskr when \u201cclimbing\u201d up and down the timeline to reach various locales.<br /> With the founding of the legacy, the founder adopted the name of the squirrel as their Shadow Name. They took to digging through the past as much as they could, collecting what legends and stories they were able. When they had gathered all that they could (which still wasn\u2019t much), they turned their efforts towards more mundane affairs: gossip, just as the great Squirrel once did. It is unknown how Ratatoskr\u2019s life ended, whether they died or ascended to some existence beyond our ken is not clear. But it is certainly clear how their activities have impacted the future legacy\u2019s reputation as liars, gossipers and tricksters.<br /> Certainly, many in the order follow in their founder\u2019s footsteps as ones who spread gossip to others. Other simply worked as messengers, while others still act as historians. The one constant is their crawling across the length of the World Tree, which can differ in appearance to some of other paths. The Obrimos tend to envision it more as Jacob\u2019s Ladder, the Mastigos as the Kabbalah or even Qlippoth, and the Moros as a skyscraper piercing through the heavens. But for most of the membership, and especially the Thyrsus and Acanthus, it remains the World Tree, and they remain as the Squirrels that make it their home.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Origins</span><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Thyrsus, Silver Ladder or Free Council<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Squirrels<br /> <b>Background:</b> Generally, any person experienced in climbing with an interest in time travel at least gives the Legacy a look at. As mentioned above, historians and messengers are the most common admissions to the Legacy, though a surprising number of members are actually comedians, clowns and other tricksters. Well, perhaps not that surprising, considering the founder\u2019s behavior.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> While the Squirrel\u2019s may not wear a hide of their namesake or eat nuts all day, they do embody the animal\u2019s nervous behavior. On the outside they tend to be cheerful pranksters, performing tricks with a grin on their face. One only needs to watch their constantly moving eyes, however, and how often their head swivels about, to see the true anxiety within. Time travel does not inherently heal wounds, and even the Legacy\u2019s attainments have their limits, and so the Squirrels are always on the lookout for when someone might consider their latest prank as one step too far. Its better to dive into the past before any damage has been done, after all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Doctrine</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 2, Athletics 2, one of the following at 2 dots: Animal Ken, Occult, Science, Stealth, Survival<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Traditionally, the Legacy was passed down by the mentor chasing the apprentice in a ritual climb across a tall tree, generally an ash tree. These days cliff faces and skyscrapers can also work, but trees are regarded as the best bet. It\u2019s also said by some Legacy members that you have to do so <i>au naturale</i> to best \u201cbring in the spirit of Ratatoskr.\u201d This is a lie, it\u2019s just a haze they do for the newcomers.<br /> <b>Organization:</b> The Squirrels have little in the way of organization beyond some agreements to help one another convey messages across the world. Besides the order\u2019s predisposition for Thyrsus members, Mastigos Squirrels are valued for their skill in teleportation, and Acanthus are also brought in for their natural inclination towards the Time Arcanum. Moros and Obrimos members tend to be less common, though not unheard of within the Legacy, as Moros convey messages through the Underworld and the Obrimos have a tendency to leave messages in runes for others to find.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magic</span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Time<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Imagery that contrasts eagles and snakes (+1), Succeeding on a Strength + Athletics roll to climb (+2), Ash tree branches and seeds (+1)<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Conveying messages between two people (can be the same person at different points in time), Spread gossip about a subject, climb a large vertical surface, carve a large hole in a vertical surface for storage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attainments<br /> First: Spotting the Eagle</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Initiation<br /> Once per chapter per person, ask the Storyteller what a target needs to hear regarding the near future, answers are one word only, but can be any word. This functions as the spell \u201cDivination\u201d with reach spent on instant casting.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 1<br /> When carrying a message for someone else, highlight the intended target within your field of vision. This functions as the spell \u201cWeb of Life\u201d with reach spent on Advanced Scale.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Second: Stability of the Trunk</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Athletics 3<br /> Traveling to and fro across the length of the World Tree is a dangerous prospect, and occasionally one must firmly grip onto its bark to avoid the erasing winds. This emulates the spell \u201cConstant Presence,\u201d with its reach spent on Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 2<br /> The Squirrel\u2019s ability to heal herself is optimized to operate within chronological travel. While traveling through time, the Squirrel can spend as much Mana as their normal Gnosis-derived limits in that turn to heal injuries or conditions, but the amount of Mana spent healing does <i>not</i> stack with Mana spent for other purposes. A Gnosis 3 Squirrel could thus travel through time, spending 3 Mana to heal their injuries while spending another 3 Mana for other effects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Third: Escaping the Serpent\u2019s Ire</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Time 3; Either increase the other required skill to 3 dots, or another required skill to 2 dots.<br /> In order to properly flee from the consequences of their actions, the Squirrel must lay false tracks along the path, to lead their pursuer astray. This emulates the spell \u201cShield of Chronos\u201d with reach spent on Advanced Duration and the false series of events.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 3<br /> Ratatoskr is one of the swiftest animals in the Nine Worlds, and the Squirrel must adopt his methods and particularly his speed in order to achieve the same results. Not only that, but taking on the Squirrel's persona leaves a mark on the mage, toughening their skin just enough that jagged bark and stone does no harm to them on the climb and on the road. A Squirrel with this attainment permanently increases their Initiative by their Life dots and gains 1/0 armor, emulating the spell \u201cBody Control.\u201d<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fourth: Falling Down the Expanse</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Time 4, Athletics 4<br /> By taking a leap of faith, the Squirrel lets go to fall into the depths of the past as a measure of safety. The Squirrel travels back in time a number of scenes equal to Time dots, retaining any Conditions or injuries they had sustained. This emulates the spell \u201cShifting Sands\u201d with the reach spent on Instant casting and full scene travel.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 4<br /> While gravity may not properly exist in the metaphor of the World Tree, a Squirrel can still draw on its symbolism to accelerate their rate of descent, thus traveling back even farther. By taking a resistant lethal wound, the Squirrel can multiply the number of scenes traveled back by (Wounds + 1), up to a maximum of Life dots. Thus, a Squirrel with Time 4 can take 2 resistant lethal wounds to multiply the number of scenes traveled back by 3, resulting in 12 scenes traveled.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fifth: Nine Worlds of Ash</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Time 5, Increase the other required skill to 4 dots, or obtain 3 dots in another required skill, or 2 dots in a third skill.<br /> The World Tree is connected to a number of different worlds, showcasing different environments and peoples within. The canny Squirrel can leave this world to enter a nearby one, altering up to their Time dots in Skill or Merit dots, moving them around as they pleased so long as they do not exceed their maximums. This emulates the spell \u201cRewrite History\u201d with reach spent on instant cast and Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 5<br /> The Squirrel can now adjust their own bodies while jumping, swapping around Attribute dots up to their Life dots. These dots cannot go below the minimum for their character creation priority, or exceed their maximum rating. In addition, the Squirrel\u2019s body while jumping can be changed to resemble any human being as they choose, emulating the spell \u201cMany Faces.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","user":"Critian Caceorte","date":". 05-10-2022, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}